From 73201443d4aee93d87e741baa57695b01049e0b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axon7-build <axon7-build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:50:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] ARM: dts: msm8996: Add ZTE Axon 7 (ailsa_ii) device tree

Port the ZTE Axon 7 (A2017G, codename ailsa_ii) board from ZTE's 3.18
kernel (zte-msm8996-v3-pmi8996-ailsa_ii.dts and the files it uses) to
this tree.

ZTE built the board by editing the CAF msm8996-mtp.dtsi and a number of
shared msm8996 dtsi files. Here:

- msm8996-zte-axon7.dtsi is the 4.4 CAF msm8996-mtp.dtsi with ZTE's
  edits applied in place: Samsung S6E3HA3 dual DSI command panel,
  microSD detect polarity, PMIC GPIO/MPP setup, volume keys on PM8994
  GPIO 2/3, NFC, AK8157 and the battery profile. The WCD9335 sound card,
  TDM interfaces and CAF reference panel overrides are left out.
- msm8996-zte-axon7-common.dtsi holds ZTE's changes to the shared files
  as overrides (pinctrl, PMI8994 charger/FG/LED/haptics, PM8994 RTC,
  L17, camera clocks, BLSP1 QUP3, AK4961/AK4490 audio nodes, MPM map,
  USB3 bus votes, BCL), so the shared dtsi stay untouched.
- Camera, Type-C, touch/keys, panel and battery profile are separate
  dtsi files taken from ZTE's sources.

Binding changes for 4.4:
- The panel 3 V rail on gpio 40, switched by ZTE's mdss driver
  (zte,lcd-3v-vsp-enable-gpio), is a fixed regulator used as the panel
  "vdd" supply with ZTE's 5 ms/2 ms delays.
- Haptics use the qcom,qpnp-haptics binding of leds-qpnp-haptics.
- Battery data lives under /vendor, as in 4.4.
- The DT fstab and vbmeta nodes are removed (first stage mount from the
  ramdisk fstab), HDMI is disabled and its splash region dropped, and
  pstore/ramoops uses the region ZTE reserved for it.

qcom,msm-id <246 0x30001>, qcom,pmic-id and qcom,board-id <100 0> match
the 3.18 DTB, so ZTE's bootloader picks it.

Add CONFIG_MACH_ZTE_AXON7. When set, only the Axon 7 DTB is built.

Nodes for hardware whose drivers are not in this tree yet (AK4961
codec, AK4490 DAC, AK8157, ISL98608, Goodix fingerprint, NDT force
sensor, PN5xx NFC, ZTE camera EEPROMs, Type-C and hall drivers until
they are added) are kept so the board description is complete.

